 climate experts and  activists are expected to attend this  year's climate summit america said cop  26 must be pivotal in tackling climate  change a pivotal moment for the world to  come together to meet and master the  climate challenge having withdrawn from  the paris agreement under donald trump  the paris accord would undermine our  economy and put us at a permanent  disadvantage it is time to exit the  paris accord the us is expected to play  a leading role at cop 26 under joe biden  we've already waited too long to deal  with this climate crisis who returned  america to the paris accord hours after  becoming president today the united  states is officially once again a party  to the paris agreement which we helped  put together the u.s and china have  butted heads in the months leading up to  cop 26. we understand that there are  problems in the relations between the us  and china a stalemate between the two  superpowers emerged as america called on  china to be more ambitious with its  targets but those problems do not  interfere with the needs to do  everything possible to make sure that  the cop is a success china is the  world's biggest greenhouse gas emitter  but insists it will pursue its own  climate goals and become carbon neutral  by 2060.  we can also expect to see some famous  faces at this year's climate summit with  the queen and the pope in attendance  you worry about the future of the planet  and what kind of award we will live for  future generations  from her majesty to climate royalty  greta tunberg had previously said she  wouldn't attend cop 26 due to safety  concerns and covet 19 vaccination  distribution  where do we want it  but the face of climate change has  changed her mind and is likely to play a  key role at the conference it's on the  school holiday so i don't have to take  time off  climate finance will be a sticking point  at cop26 generally speaking the world's  richest nations have done the most to  cause the climate crisis which is  experienced most severely by poorer  nations a group of industrialized  countries including the uk and u.s  promised to help developing countries  tackle climate change in 2009 but they  missed their targets those funds were  promised to arrive by 2020 and we are  still waiting some think finding  solutions to supporting more climate  vulnerable nations will be the key  factor in the success of cop26  but the main issue will be whether what  is agreed at cop26 will be enough to  limit the worst impacts of global  warming countries like india and  australia and china and south africa are  still struggling to agree on how to  phase out coal and whether or not they  should come forward with better more  enhanced ambitions for reducing carbon  emissions  about 10 000 officers from around the uk  will police each day of cop 26 making it  one of the biggest operations of its  kind in britain the cost of policing the  event has been estimated at around 250  million pounds police are expecting the  potentially historic event to be the  focus of large-scale demonstrations they  have been taking part in role-play  exercises to recreate protests ahead of  cop26  if cop26 goes well there could be new  alliances new emissions targets new  financial commitments made and that  would be real progress it's why there's  such pressure on cop26 and why it's been  described as the world's last best hope  to limit global warming
 

